        "topFinding": "The 11-commit burst since 2026-08-04 genuinely closed several long-chronic items (the 25-run checkout/portal userId-trust bug, a missing billing runbook, edge caching on the two hottest course-index reads), but the security lens found the matching stored-XSS fixes were committed to source and never rebuilt into the production bundle, so the vulnerability they were meant to close is still live today. Independently, three lenses converged on the same discovery: the bar-raise's own auto-enqueue step wrote zero work-queue items for the entire 2026-08-04 run despite recording roughly 55 findings that day, explaining why several chronic low scorers (Discord webhook wiring, skill-suite health, skill-chain handoff integrity) have sat untouched. That enqueue failure reproduced identically in this same run's review of Yes& Budget, confirming it as a portfolio-wide defect in the bar-raise pipeline rather than a Chains-specific gap.",
